    read: 'The twelve-month window went in one bar, the seller came back above average, and the day’s low touched the engine’s measure. Nov 20 closed 8.02 (−6.9%; the quote’s prevClose and the engine’s Nov 19 bar agree at 8.61 this time) on $153K traded — 1.11× the 20-day average ($137K) — through 8.56 (the Mar 24 low — tied Nov 19, the old +1M) by 6.3% and 8.48 (the 52-week closing low — the watch level, the last reference on the chart) by 5.4%: outside the band on both — a new 52-week and 180-day closing low, the lowest close of the series’ 365-day window. The quote’s 52-week low reads 7.756 now — the day’s low — so 7.75 (the engine’s October measure, the read’s +1M) was touched intraday and the close is 3.5% over it: not a tie on the close, and the read quotes closes. −27% from 11.04 (Nov 2) in fourteen sessions; nine red or flat bars in ten. The seller who took one day off at the March low (87%, Nov 19) came back: the sequence from Nov 12 is 1.16×, 1.44×, unsized, 1.95×, 2.73×, 87%, 1.11× — six of seven above average, every one red or flat; the 20-day average fell to $137K from $145K even as a 1.11× bar entered, so the bar that left (a late-October bounce bar) was larger still, and the window max is the Nov 18 bar ($398K), 2.6× this one. Score 0/7, STRONG BEAR, for a sixth pass: under the EMA20 (9.71 — 21% up), EMA50 (10.42), EMA100 (10.84) and EMA200 (11.15 — 39% up), all falling; MACD histogram −0.18, widening; RSI 12.9 from 25.9 — thirteen points on a −6.9% bar, as the Nov 2 bounce bar (the EMA50 touch, +4.8%) leaves the 14-day window on the day a −6.9% bar enters it: the lowest reading of the pass on this chart, the second-lowest on the page (CAI 8.7), quoted. The engine keeps the "downtrend, lower highs, no floor" frame — ceiling 14.21 (Apr 17) → 12.73 (Oct 1), ~12.3 today — and the BEAR forecast with its invalidation lowered a third time, 10.8 → 10.0, and its measure recomputed from the new low: 7.22 / 4.63 / 3.94 — its +1M the new measure, its +3M the 2-year low. Market cap ~$42M against $8.8M of cash — 4.8×. The read stays BEAR with the invalidation unchanged (12.2 — the Aug 21 high; 52% up, a structural high the convention does not reach, as written Nov 19 — the chart has no rebound top under it and every number between is a November close) and the path moved by the bar: 8.56 and 8.48 closed through, the +1M goes to 7.22 (the engine’s new measure and its +1M), 10% under, with 7.75 (the old measure — the day’s low) the step; the +3M stays 6.59 (the engine’s old +3M) with 4.63 (the 2-year low — the engine’s +3M now) behind it. The first bar the read would act on is unchanged in kind and moved in price — a hold of 7.75–8.02 with a reversal bar on tape at least as heavy as the Nov 18 bar ($398K), with the raise terms known first; the chart touched the level intraday and closed 3.5% over it on a bar that was red and above average, which is the shape of the last six bars, not of a reversal. At 4.8× cash with the twelve-month window gone, the market is pricing the raise before the company has named it, and every bar lower is a worse print to do it at.',
    pattern: '<b>Symmetrical triangle — resolved down (Oct 6–9), 90-day low lost (Oct 13), new low 9.41 (Oct 16), bounce to the sell zone (Oct 23), rejected (Oct 26), sell zone closed through (Oct 29), 10.72 lost Oct 30, EMA50 reached Nov 2 (11.04, revised bar), rejected Nov 3, shelf floor (10.43) lost Nov 5 (10.05), tested from below Nov 6 (10.35) and Nov 11 (10.22), October bounce low (9.86) lost Nov 12 (9.53, −6.8%, 1.16×), Oct 16 low tied Nov 13 (9.34, 1.44×) and Nov 16 (9.35, unsized), closed through Nov 17 (9.285, −0.7%, 1.95×), the drift resumed Nov 18 (8.84, −4.8%, 2.73× — the window max), the March low reached by a tie Nov 19 (8.61, −2.6%, 87%), the March low and the 52-week low closed through Nov 20 (8.02, −6.9%, 1.11× average volume; day low 7.756 — the engine’s measure touched) — a new 52-week closing low, RSI 13, nine red or flat bars in ten.</b> The engine draws a downtrend with no floor: ceiling 14.21 (Apr 17) → 12.73 (Oct 1), ~12.3 today; 9.41 (Oct 16) is lost and 17% overhead; 8.56 (Mar 24) and 8.48 (the old 52-week low) are lost and overhead by 6–7%; under price there is only the engine: 7.75 (its October measure — the day’s low), 7.22 (its measure now), 6.59, 4.63 (the 2-year low), 3.94. Overhead: 8.48 (the lost 52-week low — the first ceiling), 8.56 (the lost March low), 8.61 (Nov 19 close), 8.84 (Nov 18 close), 9.2 (the lost watch line), 9.285 (Nov 17 close), 9.34–9.35 (Nov 13 / Nov 16 closes), 9.41 (the Oct 16 low), 9.53 (Nov 12 close), 9.71 (EMA20), 9.86 (the lost bounce low), 10.0 (the round number / the engine’s invalidation), 10.01 (Nov 10 close), 10.05–10.06, 10.22 (Nov 11), 10.30–10.35, 10.42 (EMA50), 10.43 (the lost shelf floor), 10.72–10.85 (the old sell zone), 10.84 (EMA100), 11.04 (the shelf top), 11.15 (EMA200), 12.2 (the invalidation), 12.3, 12.73. Below: 7.75 (engine old measure — the day’s low, the step), 7.22 (engine measure / +1M — the +1M), 6.59 (engine old +3M — the +3M), 4.63 (2-year low — engine +3M), 3.94 (engine +1Y).',
    watch: '<b>7.75 and 8.48.</b> The engine’s October measure — the day’s low, 7.756 — is 3.5% under the close: a close under 7.75 (outside the band, under 7.67) on tape above the 20-day average ($137K) puts the engine’s new measure (7.22) next with nothing drawn between, and the 2-year low (4.63) behind that; a hold at 7.75–8.02 with a reversal bar on tape at least as heavy as the Nov 18 bar ($398K) is the first entry the read would write — a new 52-week low with the engine’s number under it and the raise terms the thing it needs to know first; the chart touched the level and closed 3.5% over it on a red bar above average, which is the sixth bar of that shape in seven, not the first of another. Above, 8.48–8.56 — the lost 52-week low / the lost March low — is the first ceiling, 5.7–6.7% up: a close back over 8.56 inside two sessions (Nov 23–24) makes Nov 20 a one-bar undercut of the twelve-month window; 8.61 / 8.84 (the Nov 19 / 18 closes) are the steps to 9.285–9.41 (the Nov 17 close / the lost October low), and the averages (9.71–11.15) are the frame over that. <b>Reversal needs</b> a close back above 11.2 (EMA200) and then 12.2 (Aug 21 high). <b>Volume:</b> $153K, 1.11× — the seller back above average after one day under it (87%); six of the seven bars from Nov 12 above average, all red or flat, the Nov 18 bar ($398K, 2.73×) still the window max and 2.6× this one; the 20-day average is falling ($145K → $137K) as the late-October bounce bars leave, so the same dollars read heavier each day. <b>RSI 13:</b> down thirteen points on a −6.9% bar as the Nov 2 bounce bar leaves the window — the lowest reading of the pass on this chart, quoted; oversold is the slope, not a floor (CAI has printed under 12 for four sessions and lost 12% doing it). <b>Cash $8.8M:</b> the raise is the overhang; 8.02 is a worse price to do it at than 8.61 was yesterday and 11.04 was on Nov 2, and the engine’s 7.22 is the next one — at 4.8× cash the market is pricing the terms before the company has.',
